IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `coa-definitions`
IMPORT `coa-solvency-auditors`

-- Companies Act 1967, sections 7A and 10 -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law.

§ `Fixtures -- the solvency opinion`

GIVEN `the operation` IS A ProposedOperation,
      `no ground to find it unable to pay its debts` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `intends winding up within 12 months` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `able to pay in full within 12 months of winding up` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `able to pay as they fall due for 12 months` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `assets cover liabilities now` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `assets will cover liabilities afterwards` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A SolvencyOpinion
DECIDE `an opinion` `the operation` `no ground to find it unable to pay its debts` `intends winding up within 12 months` `able to pay in full within 12 months of winding up` `able to pay as they fall due for 12 months` `assets cover liabilities now` `assets will cover liabilities afterwards` IS
    SolvencyOpinion WITH
        `the operation it is for` IS `the operation`
        `no ground on which the company could then be found to be unable to pay its debts` IS `no ground to find it unable to pay its debts`
        `it is intended to commence winding up within 12 months after the date of the statement` IS `intends winding up within 12 months`
        `the company will be able to pay its debts in full within 12 months after the commencement of the winding up` IS `able to pay in full within 12 months of winding up`
        `the company will be able to pay its debts as they fall due during the 12 months after the date of the statement` IS `able to pay as they fall due for 12 months`
        `the value of the assets is now not less than the value of the liabilities including contingent liabilities` IS `assets cover liabilities now`
        `the value of the assets will not, after the proposed operation, become less than the value of the liabilities including contingent liabilities` IS `assets will cover liabilities afterwards`

`a going concern, redeeming preference shares` MEANS `an opinion` `redemption of preference shares out of capital under section 70` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE
`a company that intends to wind up and can pay in full` MEANS `an opinion` `reduction of share capital under section 78B or 78C` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE
`a company that intends to wind up but can only pay as debts fall due` MEANS `an opinion` `reduction of share capital under section 78B or 78C` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE
`a going concern that could only pay in full on a winding up` MEANS `an opinion` `financial assistance under section 76(9A) or (9B)` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE
`a company with a ground to be found unable to pay its debts` MEANS `an opinion` `redemption of preference shares out of capital under section 70` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE
`a company whose assets are already below its liabilities` MEANS `an opinion` `redemption of preference shares out of capital under section 70` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE
`a company that would be insolvent on the balance sheet after the operation` MEANS `an opinion` `reduction of share capital under section 78B or 78C` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE
`an opinion for something the Act does not define a statement for` MEANS `an opinion` `something else` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE

§ `Section 7A(1) -- the three opinions`

#ASSERT `the directors hold all three opinions section 7A(1) requires` `a going concern, redeeming preference shares`
#ASSERT `the directors hold all three opinions section 7A(1) requires` `a company that intends to wind up and can pay in full`

-- Limb (b) forks on intention. The same two facts, with the intention to wind up
-- switched, give different answers.
#ASSERT `limb (b) of the opinion is held` `a going concern, redeeming preference shares`
#ASSERT NOT `limb (b) of the opinion is held` `a company that intends to wind up but can only pay as debts fall due`
#ASSERT NOT `the directors hold all three opinions section 7A(1) requires` `a company that intends to wind up but can only pay as debts fall due`
#ASSERT NOT `limb (b) of the opinion is held` `a going concern that could only pay in full on a winding up`
#ASSERT NOT `the directors hold all three opinions section 7A(1) requires` `a going concern that could only pay in full on a winding up`

-- Limbs (a) and (c), including the forward-looking half of (c).
#ASSERT NOT `the directors hold all three opinions section 7A(1) requires` `a company with a ground to be found unable to pay its debts`
#ASSERT NOT `the directors hold all three opinions section 7A(1) requires` `a company whose assets are already below its liabilities`
#ASSERT NOT `the directors hold all three opinions section 7A(1) requires` `a company that would be insolvent on the balance sheet after the operation`

-- Only three operations are provided for.
#ASSERT `the operation is one a solvency statement is defined for` `a going concern, redeeming preference shares`
#ASSERT `the operation is one a solvency statement is defined for` `a company that intends to wind up and can pay in full`
#ASSERT `the operation is one a solvency statement is defined for` `a going concern that could only pay in full on a winding up`
#ASSERT NOT `the operation is one a solvency statement is defined for` `an opinion for something the Act does not define a statement for`

§ `Section 7A(2) -- the form`

GIVEN `exempt from audit` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `directors` IS A NUMBER,
      `signed` IS A NUMBER,
      `auditor's report` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A StatementForm
DECIDE `a form` `exempt from audit` `directors` `signed` `auditor's report` IS
    StatementForm WITH
        `the company is exempt from audit requirements under section 205B or 205C` IS `exempt from audit`
        `the number of directors` IS `directors`
        `the number of directors who signed the written declaration` IS `signed`
        `an auditor's report accompanies it saying the auditor has inquired into the company's affairs and thinks the statement not unreasonable` IS `auditor's report`

`an audit-exempt company, all three directors sign` MEANS `a form` TRUE 3 3 FALSE
`an audit-exempt company, two of three sign, with an auditor's report` MEANS `a form` TRUE 3 2 TRUE
`an audit-exempt company, two of three sign` MEANS `a form` TRUE 3 2 FALSE
`an audited company, all three directors sign` MEANS `a form` FALSE 3 3 FALSE
`an audited company, two of three sign, with an auditor's report` MEANS `a form` FALSE 3 2 TRUE
`an audited company, two of three sign, no report` MEANS `a form` FALSE 3 2 FALSE
`an audit-exempt company with a sole director who signs` MEANS `a form` TRUE 1 1 FALSE

#ASSERT `every director signed` `an audit-exempt company, all three directors sign`
#ASSERT `the statement is in a form section 7A(2) allows` `an audit-exempt company, all three directors sign`
#ASSERT `the statement is in a form section 7A(2) allows` `an audited company, all three directors sign`
#ASSERT `the statement is in a form section 7A(2) allows` `an audit-exempt company with a sole director who signs`

-- THE ASYMMETRY. With two of three signatures and an auditor's report, the audited
-- company is in and the audit-exempt company is out. The small company has fewer ways
-- to give the statement.
#ASSERT `the statement is in a form section 7A(2) allows` `an audited company, two of three sign, with an auditor's report`
#ASSERT NOT `the statement is in a form section 7A(2) allows` `an audit-exempt company, two of three sign, with an auditor's report`
#ASSERT NOT `the statement is in a form section 7A(2) allows` `an audit-exempt company, two of three sign`
#ASSERT NOT `the statement is in a form section 7A(2) allows` `an audited company, two of three sign, no report`

§ `Section 7A(3), (4) -- how the opinion is formed`

GIVEN `all liabilities` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `financial statements` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `other circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `relied on reasonable valuations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A HowTheOpinionWasFormed
DECIDE `a method` `all liabilities` `financial statements` `other circumstances` `relied on reasonable valuations` IS
    HowTheOpinionWasFormed WITH
        `took into account all liabilities including contingent liabilities` IS `all liabilities`
        `had regard to the most recent financial statements complying with section 201(2) and (5)` IS `financial statements`
        `had regard to all other circumstances the directors know or ought to know affect the value of assets and liabilities` IS `other circumstances`
        `relied on valuations or estimates that were reasonable in the circumstances` IS `relied on reasonable valuations`

`every step taken` MEANS `a method` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
`every step taken without relying on any valuation` MEANS `a method` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE
`contingent liabilities left out` MEANS `a method` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE
`the latest financial statements not consulted` MEANS `a method` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE
`known circumstances ignored` MEANS `a method` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE

#ASSERT `the directors went about forming the opinion as section 7A(3) and (4)(a) require` `every step taken`

-- s 7A(4)(b) says the directors "may" rely on reasonable valuations. It is a permission,
-- not a requirement.
#ASSERT `the directors went about forming the opinion as section 7A(3) and (4)(a) require` `every step taken without relying on any valuation`

#ASSERT NOT `the directors went about forming the opinion as section 7A(3) and (4)(a) require` `contingent liabilities left out`
#ASSERT NOT `the directors went about forming the opinion as section 7A(3) and (4)(a) require` `the latest financial statements not consulted`
#ASSERT NOT `the directors went about forming the opinion as section 7A(3) and (4)(a) require` `known circumstances ignored`

§ `Section 7A(6) -- the offence`

GIVEN `made it` IS A BOOLEAN, `had reasonable grounds` IS A BOOLEAN, `later insolvent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DirectorsStatement
DECIDE `a director` `made it` `had reasonable grounds` `later insolvent` IS
    DirectorsStatement WITH
        `this director made the solvency statement` IS `made it`
        `this director had reasonable grounds for the opinions expressed in it` IS `had reasonable grounds`
        `the company later became insolvent` IS `later insolvent`

`a director who signed without reasonable grounds` MEANS `a director` TRUE FALSE FALSE
`a director who signed without reasonable grounds, and the company failed` MEANS `a director` TRUE FALSE TRUE
`a director who signed on reasonable grounds` MEANS `a director` TRUE TRUE FALSE
`a director who signed on reasonable grounds, and the company failed anyway` MEANS `a director` TRUE TRUE TRUE
`a director who did not sign` MEANS `a director` FALSE FALSE FALSE

#ASSERT `the director commits the offence in section 7A(6)` `a director who signed without reasonable grounds`
#ASSERT NOT `the director commits the offence in section 7A(6)` `a director who signed on reasonable grounds`
#ASSERT NOT `the director commits the offence in section 7A(6)` `a director who did not sign`

-- Later insolvency is not an element. The offence turns on the grounds when the
-- statement was made, so a failure does not convict a director who had good grounds and a
-- success does not acquit one who had none.
#ASSERT `the director commits the offence in section 7A(6)` `a director who signed without reasonable grounds, and the company failed`
#ASSERT NOT `the director commits the offence in section 7A(6)` `a director who signed on reasonable grounds, and the company failed anyway`
#ASSERT NOT `a later insolvency is an element of the offence`

#ASSERT `the maximum fine under section 7A(6), in dollars` EQUALS 100000
#ASSERT `the maximum imprisonment under section 7A(6), in months` EQUALS 36

§ `Section 10(1), (2) -- who may be an auditor`

#ASSERT `the person is an accounting entity` `a public accountant`
#ASSERT `the person is an accounting entity` `an accounting corporation`
#ASSERT `the person is an accounting entity` `an accounting firm`
#ASSERT `the person is an accounting entity` `an accounting limited liability partnership`
#ASSERT NOT `the person is an accounting entity` `not an accounting entity`

-- Both prohibitions carry "knowingly".
#ASSERT `the person contravenes section 10(1)` `not an accounting entity` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the person contravenes section 10(1)` `not an accounting entity` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the person contravenes section 10(1)` `a public accountant` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the person contravenes section 10(1)` `an accounting firm` TRUE

#ASSERT `the person acted as an auditor` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the person acted as an auditor` FALSE

§ `Fixtures -- consents`

GIVEN `who` IS AN Auditor,
      `in writing` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `signed by the public accountant` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `partners who signed` IS A NUMBER,
      `directors who signed` IS A NUMBER,
      `before the appointment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Consent
DECIDE `a consent` `who` `in writing` `signed by the public accountant` `partners who signed` `directors who signed` `before the appointment` IS
    Consent WITH
        `who is being appointed` IS `who`
        `it is in writing` IS `in writing`
        `it was signed by the public accountant` IS `signed by the public accountant`
        `the number of partners who signed` IS `partners who signed`
        `the number of directors who signed` IS `directors who signed`
        `it was obtained before the appointment` IS `before the appointment`

`a public accountant's signed written consent` MEANS `a consent` `a public accountant` TRUE TRUE 0 0 TRUE
`a public accountant's unsigned consent` MEANS `a consent` `a public accountant` TRUE FALSE 0 0 TRUE
`a firm's consent signed by one partner` MEANS `a consent` `an accounting firm` TRUE FALSE 1 0 TRUE
`a firm's consent signed by no partner` MEANS `a consent` `an accounting firm` TRUE FALSE 0 0 TRUE
`a firm's consent signed by a director instead` MEANS `a consent` `an accounting firm` TRUE FALSE 0 1 TRUE
`a limited liability partnership's consent signed by one partner` MEANS `a consent` `an accounting limited liability partnership` TRUE FALSE 1 0 TRUE
`a corporation's consent signed by one director` MEANS `a consent` `an accounting corporation` TRUE FALSE 0 1 TRUE
`a corporation's consent signed by a partner instead` MEANS `a consent` `an accounting corporation` TRUE FALSE 3 0 TRUE
`a consent that is not in writing` MEANS `a consent` `an accounting firm` FALSE FALSE 1 0 TRUE
`a consent obtained after the appointment` MEANS `a consent` `an accounting firm` TRUE FALSE 1 0 FALSE
`a consent from someone who is not an accounting entity` MEANS `a consent` `not an accounting entity` TRUE TRUE 1 1 TRUE

§ `Section 10(3), (4) -- prior consent`

#ASSERT `the appointment complies with section 10(3) and (4)` `a public accountant's signed written consent`
#ASSERT NOT `the appointment complies with section 10(3) and (4)` `a public accountant's unsigned consent`

#ASSERT `the appointment complies with section 10(3) and (4)` `a firm's consent signed by one partner`
#ASSERT NOT `the appointment complies with section 10(3) and (4)` `a firm's consent signed by no partner`

-- The signatory must be the right kind of person for the entity: a director cannot
-- sign for a firm, nor a partner for a corporation.
#ASSERT NOT `the appointment complies with section 10(3) and (4)` `a firm's consent signed by a director instead`
#ASSERT NOT `the appointment complies with section 10(3) and (4)` `a corporation's consent signed by a partner instead`
#ASSERT `the appointment complies with section 10(3) and (4)` `a corporation's consent signed by one director`

-- An accounting limited liability partnership is treated like a firm for the consent.
#ASSERT `the appointment complies with section 10(3) and (4)` `a limited liability partnership's consent signed by one partner`

#ASSERT NOT `the appointment complies with section 10(3) and (4)` `a consent that is not in writing`
#ASSERT NOT `the appointment complies with section 10(3) and (4)` `a consent obtained after the appointment`
#ASSERT NOT `the appointment complies with section 10(3) and (4)` `a consent from someone who is not an accounting entity`

§ `Fixtures -- practitioners`

GIVEN `role` IS A Practitioner,
      `practising now` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `held the role at the time of the appointment` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `a public accountant at the time of the appointment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A PractitionerFacts
DECIDE `a practitioner` `role` `practising now` `held the role at the time of the appointment` `a public accountant at the time of the appointment` IS
    PractitionerFacts WITH
        `role` IS `role`
        `is practising as a public accountant in the entity now` IS `practising now`
        `held that role at the time of the appointment` IS `held the role at the time of the appointment`
        `was a public accountant at the time of the appointment` IS `a public accountant at the time of the appointment`

`a partner of the firm throughout, a public accountant throughout` MEANS `a practitioner` `a partner of the accounting firm` TRUE TRUE TRUE
`a partner who joined the firm after the appointment` MEANS `a practitioner` `a partner of the accounting firm` TRUE FALSE TRUE
`a partner who qualified as a public accountant after the appointment` MEANS `a practitioner` `a partner of the accounting firm` TRUE TRUE FALSE
`a director of the corporation throughout` MEANS `a practitioner` `a director of the accounting corporation` TRUE TRUE TRUE
`a director who joined the corporation after the appointment` MEANS `a practitioner` `a director of the accounting corporation` TRUE FALSE TRUE
`an employee who joined the corporation after the appointment` MEANS `a practitioner` `an employee of the accounting corporation` TRUE FALSE TRUE
`an employee of the corporation who does not practise` MEANS `a practitioner` `an employee of the accounting corporation` FALSE TRUE FALSE
`a partner of an accounting limited liability partnership` MEANS `a practitioner` `a partner of the accounting limited liability partnership` TRUE TRUE TRUE

§ `Section 10(5), (6) -- who is appointed when a firm or a corporation is appointed in its own name`

-- s 10(5): the firm's partners AT THE TIME of the appointment, who are public accountants
-- AT THAT TIME.
#ASSERT `the practitioner is appointed as an auditor through the entity` `a partner of the firm throughout, a public accountant throughout` `an accounting firm`
#ASSERT NOT `the practitioner is appointed as an auditor through the entity` `a partner who joined the firm after the appointment` `an accounting firm`
#ASSERT NOT `the practitioner is appointed as an auditor through the entity` `a partner who qualified as a public accountant after the appointment` `an accounting firm`

-- s 10(6): the corporation's directors and employees "whether ... at the time ... or later".
#ASSERT `the practitioner is appointed as an auditor through the entity` `a director of the corporation throughout` `an accounting corporation`
#ASSERT `the practitioner is appointed as an auditor through the entity` `a director who joined the corporation after the appointment` `an accounting corporation`
#ASSERT `the practitioner is appointed as an auditor through the entity` `an employee who joined the corporation after the appointment` `an accounting corporation`
#ASSERT NOT `the practitioner is appointed as an auditor through the entity` `an employee of the corporation who does not practise` `an accounting corporation`

-- THE ASYMMETRY. Someone who joins after the appointment is an auditor of the company
-- if they join the corporation and is not if they join the firm.
#ASSERT `the practitioner is appointed as an auditor through the entity` `a director who joined the corporation after the appointment` `an accounting corporation`
#ASSERT NOT `the practitioner is appointed as an auditor through the entity` `a partner who joined the firm after the appointment` `an accounting firm`

-- THE GAP. An accounting limited liability partnership is an accounting entity and can
-- consent, but neither s 10(5) nor s 10(6) says who is appointed when it is appointed in
-- its own name.
#ASSERT NOT `the practitioner is appointed as an auditor through the entity` `a partner of an accounting limited liability partnership` `an accounting limited liability partnership`
#ASSERT NOT `section 10 says who is appointed when an accounting limited liability partnership is appointed in its own name`

-- A public accountant appointed personally is outside both subsections.
#ASSERT NOT `the practitioner is appointed as an auditor through the entity` `a partner of the firm throughout, a public accountant throughout` `a public accountant`
